1
00:00:00,707 --> 00:00:02,957
(Raj:)...mixer for grad students
and faculty...

2
00:00:03,126 --> 00:00:05,466
(Raj:)...of the Science
and Humanities Departments.

3
00:00:05,629 --> 00:00:10,549
(Raj:)Whether you split atoms or infinitives,
this is the place to be."

4
00:00:11,051 --> 00:00:13,551
(Sheldon:)Well, that's certainly amusing...

5
00:00:14,387 --> 00:00:15,847
(Sheldon:)...but I have no interest.

6
00:00:16,264 --> 00:00:17,304
(Raj:)Come on, Sheldon.

7
00:00:17,474 --> 00:00:19,974
(Raj:)The world is filled with people
doing things outside.

8
00:00:20,143 --> 00:00:22,813
(Raj:)Let's go outside. Outside is good.

9
00:00:22,979 --> 00:00:24,519
(Sheldon:)If outside is so good...

10
00:00:24,689 --> 00:00:28,399
(Sheldon:)...why has mankind spent thousands
of years trying to perfect inside?

11
00:00:29,236 --> 00:00:31,566
(Raj:)I don't know. It's a marketing scheme.

12
00:00:32,239 --> 00:00:35,409
(Raj:)Please, Sheldon, I'm a young,
virile visitor from a foreign land...

13
00:00:35,575 --> 00:00:38,915
(Raj:)...and I need to strut my stuff.

14
00:00:39,371 --> 00:00:41,161
(Sheldon:)Let me offer you a compromise.

15
00:00:41,331 --> 00:00:45,041
(Sheldon:)Sometimes when I feel stifled
and want a change of scenery...

16
00:00:45,210 --> 00:00:47,840
(Sheldon:)...I use my imagination.

17
00:00:48,004 --> 00:00:49,044
(Raj:)Oh, boy.

18
00:00:49,214 --> 00:00:52,594
One of my favorite places to visit
is the two-dimensional world...

19
00:00:52,759 --> 00:00:56,549
(Sheldon:)...described in Edwin Abbott's
mathematical fantasy Flatland.

20
00:00:57,347 --> 00:00:59,177
I don't wanna go to Flatland.

